---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { brand } from '../config/brand';
---
<Base title="Terms" description="The terms: the tools are free, the numbers are examples, and nothing here is advice.">
  <div class="lexjolt-shell lj-page" style="max-width:760px">
    <p class="lexjolt-eyebrow">Terms</p>
    <h1 class="lexjolt-h1">Free tools, no advice</h1>

    <h2 class="lexjolt-h2" style="margin-top:24px">1. What this is</h2>
    <p class="lj-lede-sm">
      LexJolt provides calculators, measurements and templates for educational use. They are not
      financial, legal, tax or investment advice, and using them does not create any professional
      relationship.
    </p>

    <h2 class="lexjolt-h2" style="margin-top:24px">2. The numbers are examples</h2>
    <p class="lj-lede-sm">
      Default inputs are plausible examples chosen to make the arithmetic legible. They are not market
      data, not a recommendation, and not a forecast. A result is a function of the inputs you supply;
      if an input is wrong, the answer is wrong, and the tool cannot tell.
    </p>

    <h2 class="lexjolt-h2" style="margin-top:24px">3. No warranty</h2>
    <p class="lj-lede-sm">
      The tools are provided as-is, without warranty of any kind. Formulas follow standard practice and
      are gated against a reference implementation, but tax rules, lending standards and market
      conditions vary by jurisdiction and change. Verify anything material with a qualified
      professional before you act on it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="lexjolt-h2" style="margin-top:24px">4. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p class="lj-lede-sm">
      Use the tools and the videos for anything lawful, including commercial content, with or without
      attribution. Do not present the outputs as advice given by {brand.name}, do not scrape the site in
      a way that degrades it for others, and do not misrepresent a computed example as market data.
    </p>

    <h2 class="lexjolt-h2" style="margin-top:24px">5. Changes</h2>
    <p class="lj-lede-sm">
      These terms may change; the date below is the version in force. Continued use after a change
      means you accept the new version.
    </p>

    <p class="lj-note" style="margin-top:24px">Version: {new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)}</p>
  </div>
</Base>
